  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Murrayatin and the CD276 antigen, mediated through the DNA polymerase iota enzyme. Three distinct pathways highlight this connection, with Murrayatin acting as a target for multiple compounds that ultimately interact with CD276 antigen. These compounds—2-((4-(Ethylamino)-6-methoxy-1,3,5-triazin-2-yl)amino)-2-methylpropiononitrile, (6S,10S)-6,10,14-trimethylpentadecan-2-one, and Guangsangon K—each target DNA polymerase iota, which in turn is recognized by the CD276 antigen. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a plausible biological link, though the exact mechanism of interaction between Murrayatin and DNA polymerase iota remains unclear. The evidence supports a hierarchical pathway where Murrayatin may influence the activity of DNA polymerase iota, which then interacts with CD276 antigen, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
